<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_ClearTotalizer1" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output to Clear Totalizer1 to Meter]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_HasDensity" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[0 = Magnetic Flowmeter, 1 = Coriolis Mass Flowmeter (reports density, etc.)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_InpDINT" DataType="DINT" Radix="Hex" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Input REAL bit pattern as a DINT (check for Inf/NaN)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Hex" Value="16#0000_0000"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_SrcQ" DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Register for building Source / Quality enumeration]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
I/O / INSTRUMENTATION -- E+H Promass 100 Magnetic Flowmeter
on EtherNet/IP (with Firmware 1.x)
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V3.0-00  2013-10-30:  Updated to Library of Premier Integration Objects V3.0.
V3.0-01  2014-01-22:  Backported to V18 of RSLogix 5000.
V3.0-02  2014-02-28:  Corrected default value of Inf_Type (local string)
V3.0-03  2014-04-04:  Add checking for Infinite / NaN on REAL input values.
V3.1-00  2014-07-09:  Added SrcQ enumerations.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
This Instruction manages a Promass 100 Flowmeter with EtherNet/IP.  It:
* Allows clearing the three totalizers
* Makes available the Mass Flow, Mass Total, Volume Flow,
and Volume Total of the stream

NOTE: This AOI is for use with meters with Version 1.x Firmware!
There is a separate AOI for use with Version 2.x Firmware.
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==================================================================
CLEAR TOTALIZERS 1-3
==================================================================
If a CLEAR TOT Command is received, send the Reset Totalizer command to the meter.
When the Totalizer has been reset (< Zero Threshold), clear the meter command.

CLEAR TOTALIZER 1

This rung checks the bit pattern of the REAL input (by copying to a DINT) to see if
the input is +Infinity, -Infinity or Not a Number.  Per ANSI 32-bit Float
format, in these cases the Exponent bits (.30 thru .23) will all be 1s:
0111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = +Infinity
1111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = -Infinity
x111 1111 1xxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx = Not a Number

#####  V3.0-03  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on REAL input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)OTL(Rdy_ClearTotalizer1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Totalizer1,Val_Totalizer1,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Totalizer1,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)JMP(SkipTot1Cmp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(Val_Totalizer1,Cfg_Totalizer1_ZeroThresh)OTU(Rdy_ClearTotalizer1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipTot1Cmp)XIO(Rdy_ClearTotalizer1)OTU(Wrk_ClearTotalizer1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_ClearTotalizer1) ,XIC(PCmd_ClearTotalizer1) ]OTU(OCmd_ClearTotalizer1)OTU(PCmd_ClearTotalizer1)OTL(Wrk_ClearTotalizer1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ClearTotalizer1)OTE(Ref_Output.Totalizer_Control_1_Activation)MOV(198,Ref_Output.Totalizer_1_Control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_ClearTotalizer1)MOV(0,Ref_Output.Totalizer_1_Control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CLEAR TOTALIZER 2

If a CLEAR TOT Command is received, send the Reset Totalizer command to the meter.
When the Totalizer has been reset (< Zero Threshold), clear the meter command.

#####  V3.0-03  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on REAL input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(Rdy_ClearTotalizer2)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Totalizer2,Val_Totalizer2,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Totalizer2,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)JMP(SkipTot2Cmp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(Val_Totalizer2,Cfg_Totalizer2_ZeroThresh)OTU(Rdy_ClearTotalizer2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipTot2Cmp)XIO(Rdy_ClearTotalizer2)OTU(Wrk_ClearTotalizer2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_ClearTotalizer2) ,XIC(PCmd_ClearTotalizer2) ]OTU(OCmd_ClearTotalizer2)OTU(PCmd_ClearTotalizer2)OTL(Wrk_ClearTotalizer2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ClearTotalizer2)OTE(Ref_Output.Totalizer_Control_2_Activation)MOV(198,Ref_Output.Totalizer_2_Control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_ClearTotalizer2)MOV(0,Ref_Output.Totalizer_2_Control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CLEAR TOTALIZER 3

If a CLEAR TOT Command is received, send the Reset Totalizer command to the meter.
When the Totalizer has been reset (< Zero Threshold), clear the meter command.

#####  V3.0-03  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on REAL input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(Rdy_ClearTotalizer3)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Totalizer3,Val_Totalizer3,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Totalizer3,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)JMP(SkipTot3Cmp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(Val_Totalizer3,Cfg_Totalizer3_ZeroThresh)OTU(Rdy_ClearTotalizer3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipTot3Cmp)XIO(Rdy_ClearTotalizer3)OTU(Wrk_ClearTotalizer3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_ClearTotalizer3) ,XIC(PCmd_ClearTotalizer3) ]OTU(OCmd_ClearTotalizer3)OTU(PCmd_ClearTotalizer3)OTL(Wrk_ClearTotalizer3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ClearTotalizer3)OTE(Ref_Output.Totalizer_Control_3_Activation)MOV(198,Ref_Output.Totalizer_3_Control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_ClearTotalizer3)MOV(0,Ref_Output.Totalizer_3_Control);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[====================================================================================
PROCESS VALUES
====================================================================================

This rung reports the current values for MASS FLOW, VOLUME FLOW and CORRECTED VOLUME FLOW.

#####  V3.0-03  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on REAL input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Mass_Flow,Val_MassFlow,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Volume_Flow,Val_VolumeFlow,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Corrected_Volume_Flow,Val_CorVolFlow,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reports the current values for  DENSITY, CORRECTED DENSITY and TEMPERATURE.

#####  V3.0-03  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on REAL input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Density,Val_Density,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Reference_Density,Val_CorDensity,1)COP(Ref_Input.Process_variables_Temperature,Val_Temp,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
====================================================================================
PROCESS VALUE UNIT CODES
====================================================================================


This rung reports the current unit code for MASS FLOW.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitMassFlow,Val_MassFlowUnit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reports the current unit code for VOLUME FLOW.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitVolumeFlow,Val_VolumeFlowUnit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reports the current unit code for CORRECTED VOLUME FLOW.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitCorrVolumeFlow,Val_CorrVolFlowUnit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reports the current unit code for DENSITY.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitDensity,Val_DensityUnit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reports the current unit code for REFERENCE DENSITY.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitRefDensity,Val_RefDensityUnit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reports the current unit code for TEMPERATURE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitTemperature,Val_TempUnit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==============================================================
Device System Condition and Connection Loss
=============================================================
Use System Condition from Instrument when Connection Status is Good]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Ref_Input.Status_Actual_diagnostics,Val_ActualSysConditionCode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Ref_Input.Connection_Fault) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_PVBad);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GEQ(Val_ActualSysConditionCode,2)OTE(Sts_PVUncertain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
====================================================================================
PROCESS VALUE UNIT DESCRIPTIONS
====================================================================================

Mass Flow Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_EUMassRateFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_EUMassRateFSC) FSC(Wrk_EUMassRateFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_EUMassRateFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.SystemUnitMassFlow) ,XIC(Wrk_EUMassRateFSC.FD) [COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_EUMassRateFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUDevMassFlow,1) ,COP(Ref_Config.SystemUnitMassFlow,Val_EUMassFlowCodeOut,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UserEUSel1) COP(Val_EUDevMassFlow,Val_EUMassFlow,1) ] ,XIC(Cfg_UserEUSel1) COP(Cfg_UserEU1,Val_EUMassFlow,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitMassFlow,Val_EUMassFlowCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Volume Flow Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_EUVolRateFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_EUVolRateFSC) FSC(Wrk_EUVolRateFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_EUVolRateFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.SystemUnitVolume) ,XIC(Wrk_EUVolRateFSC.FD) [COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_EUVolRateFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUDevVolFlow,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UserEUSel2) COP(Val_EUDevVolFlow,Val_EUVolFlow,1) ] ,XIC(Cfg_UserEUSel2) COP(Cfg_UserEU2,Val_EUVolFlow,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitVolumeFlow,Val_EUVolFlowCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Corrected Volume Flow Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_EUCorrVolRateFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_EUCorrVolRateFSC) FSC(Wrk_EUCorrVolRateFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_EUCorrVolRateFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.SystemUnitCorrVolumeFlow) ,XIC(Wrk_EUCorrVolRateFSC.FD) [COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_EUCorrVolRateFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUDevCorrVolFlow,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UserEUSel3) COP(Val_EUDevCorrVolFlow,Val_EUCorrVolFlow,1) ] ,XIC(Cfg_UserEUSel3) COP(Cfg_UserEU3,Val_EUCorrVolFlow,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitCorrVolumeFlow,Val_EUCorrVolFlowCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Density Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_EUDensityFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_EUDensityFSC) FSC(Wrk_EUDensityFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_EUDensityFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.SystemUnitDensity) ,XIC(Wrk_EUDensityFSC.FD) [COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_EUDensityFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUDevDensity,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UserEUSel4) COP(Val_EUDevDensity,Val_EUDensity,1) ] ,XIC(Cfg_UserEUSel4) COP(Cfg_UserEU4,Val_EUDensity,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitDensity,Val_EUDensityCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reference Density Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_EURefDensityFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_EURefDensityFSC) FSC(Wrk_EURefDensityFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_EURefDensityFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.SystemUnitRefDensity) ,XIC(Wrk_EURefDensityFSC.FD) [COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_EURefDensityFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUDevRefDensity,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UserEUSel5) COP(Val_EUDevRefDensity,Val_EURefDensity,1) ] ,XIC(Cfg_UserEUSel5) COP(Cfg_UserEU5,Val_EURefDensity,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitRefDensity,Val_EURefDensityCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Temperature Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_EUTempFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_EUTempFSC) FSC(Wrk_EUTempFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_EUTempFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.SystemUnitTemperature) ,XIC(Wrk_EUTempFSC.FD) [COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_EUTempFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUDevTemp,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UserEUSel6) COP(Val_EUDevTemp,Val_EUTemp,1) ] ,XIC(Cfg_UserEUSel6) COP(Cfg_UserEU6,Val_EUTemp,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.SystemUnitTemperature,Val_EUTempCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Totalizer 1 Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_Tot1AssignFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_Tot1AssignFSC) FSC(Wrk_Tot1AssignFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot1AssignFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.Totalizer1_Assign) ,XIC(Wrk_Tot1AssignFSC.FD) COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot1AssignFSC.POS].Desc,Val_Tot1AssignDesc,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.Totalizer1_Assign,Val_Total1_AssignCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_Tot1UFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_Tot1UFSC) FSC(Wrk_Tot1UFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot1UFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.Totalizer1_Unit) ,XIC(Wrk_Tot1UFSC.FD) COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot1UFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUTot1Desc,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Totalizer 2 Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_Tot2AssignFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_Tot2AssignFSC) FSC(Wrk_Tot2AssignFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot2AssignFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.Totalizer2_Assign) ,XIC(Wrk_Tot2AssignFSC.FD) COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot2AssignFSC.POS].Desc,Val_Tot2AssignDesc,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.Totalizer2_Assign,Val_Total2_AssignCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_Tot2UFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_Tot2UFSC) FSC(Wrk_Tot2UFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot2UFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.Totalizer2_Unit) ,XIC(Wrk_Tot2UFSC.FD) COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot2UFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUTot2Desc,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Totalizer 3 Units]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_Tot3AssignFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_Tot3AssignFSC) FSC(Wrk_Tot3AssignFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot3AssignFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.Totalizer3_Assign) ,XIC(Wrk_Tot3AssignFSC.FD) COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot3AssignFSC.POS].Desc,Val_Tot3AssignDesc,1) ,MOV(Ref_Config.Totalizer3_Assign,Val_Total3_AssignCode) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_EU,0,Wrk_Tot3UFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_Tot3UFSC) FSC(Wrk_Tot3UFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot3UFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Config.Totalizer3_Unit) ,XIC(Wrk_Tot3UFSC.FD) COP(Ref_EU[Wrk_Tot3UFSC.POS].Desc,Val_EUTot3Desc,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[System Conditions]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[SIZE(Ref_SysCondition,0,Wrk_SysConFSC.LEN) ,RES(Wrk_SysConFSC) FSC(Wrk_SysConFSC,?,?,ALL,Ref_SysCondition[Wrk_SysConFSC.POS].Code=Ref_Input.Status_Actual_diagnostics) ,COP(Ref_Input.Status_Actual_diagnostics,Val_ActualSysConditionCode,1) ,XIC(Wrk_SysConFSC.FD) COP(Ref_SysCondition[Wrk_SysConFSC.POS].Desc,Val_ActualSysCondition,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Sts_PVUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Sts_PVBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(Inf_HasDensity);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_32"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="P_EUTable_EIP"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="P_FaultTable"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
